<%!--
  The one text that says which `$all` positions a query matches. `Statements.query_positions`
  renders it for two hosts: a plain statement (schema-qualified tables, `$n::type` expressions)
  and a PL/pgSQL body (no prefix, its `search_path` is set, `p_*` names). Keep it free of
  anything only one host can run.

  One probe per row of the arrays, and one arm per probe shape: tag and type, tag only, type
  only. Each arm's first columns are an index's, so a probe costs what its own hits cost.

  The `stream_events` check sits before the limit on purpose: a tag or type row with no `$all`
  row must neither be returned nor use up the limit. A hard delete removes both together, but
  an old pod's hard delete, or a raw delete of events outside the store, as an application's
  orphan sweep is, can still leave such a row behind.

  `OFFSET 0` keeps each check a per-row index probe: it stops the planner flattening the check
  into a join or hashing the whole table, which a probe under the `$all` lock must never do.

  The per-probe limit is sound. A position in the top N of the union is in the top N of every
  probe that matches it, because a probe's positions are a subset of the union's. So cutting
  each probe at N loses no position of the top N, and no probe of such a position either, which
  is what keeps `matched_items` complete.
--%>
SELECT probe.item, hit.position
FROM unnest(<%= items %>, <%= tags %>, <%= types %>) AS probe (item, tag, event_type)
CROSS JOIN LATERAL (
  (
    SELECT t1.position
    FROM <%= prefix %>event_tags t1
    WHERE probe.tag IS NOT NULL AND probe.event_type IS NOT NULL
      AND t1.tag = probe.tag COLLATE "C"
      AND t1.event_type = probe.event_type COLLATE "C"
      AND t1.position <%= op %> <%= bound %>
      AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM <%= prefix %>stream_events se
        WHERE se.stream_id = 0 AND se.stream_version = t1.position
        OFFSET 0
      )
      AND NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM unnest(<%= rest_items %>, <%= rest_tags %>) AS rest (item, tag)
        WHERE rest.item = probe.item
          AND NOT EXISTS (
            SELECT 1
            FROM <%= prefix %>event_tags t2
            WHERE t2.tag = rest.tag COLLATE "C" AND t2.position = t1.position
            OFFSET 0
          )
      )
    ORDER BY t1.position <%= order %>
    LIMIT <%= limit %>
  )
  UNION ALL
  (
    SELECT t1.position
    FROM <%= prefix %>event_tags t1
    WHERE probe.tag IS NOT NULL AND probe.event_type IS NULL
      AND t1.tag = probe.tag COLLATE "C"
      AND t1.position <%= op %> <%= bound %>
      AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM <%= prefix %>stream_events se
        WHERE se.stream_id = 0 AND se.stream_version = t1.position
        OFFSET 0
      )
      AND NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM unnest(<%= rest_items %>, <%= rest_tags %>) AS rest (item, tag)
        WHERE rest.item = probe.item
          AND NOT EXISTS (
            SELECT 1
            FROM <%= prefix %>event_tags t2
            WHERE t2.tag = rest.tag COLLATE "C" AND t2.position = t1.position
            OFFSET 0
          )
      )
    ORDER BY t1.position <%= order %>
    LIMIT <%= limit %>
  )
  UNION ALL
  (
    SELECT e1.position
    FROM <%= prefix %>event_types e1
    WHERE probe.tag IS NULL
      AND e1.event_type = probe.event_type COLLATE "C"
      AND e1.position <%= op %> <%= bound %>
      AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM <%= prefix %>stream_events se
        WHERE se.stream_id = 0 AND se.stream_version = e1.position
        OFFSET 0
      )
    ORDER BY e1.position <%= order %>
    LIMIT <%= limit %>
  )
) AS hit
